==English==
{{wp}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ɪkˈspɹɛs/|/ɛkˈspɹɛs/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-express.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɛs|s=2}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{bor|en|fr|exprès}}, from {{der|en|la|expressus}}, past participle of {{m|la|exprimere}} (see [[#Etymology 2|Etymology 2]], below).

====Adjective====
{{en-adj}}

# {{lb|en|not comparable}} Moving or operating quickly, as a train not making local stops.
#: {{syn|en|fast|crack}}
# {{lb|en|comparable}} [[specific|Specific]] or [[precise]]; directly and distinctly stated; not merely [[implied]].
#: {{syn|en|explicit|plain|Thesaurus:explicit}}
#: {{ant|en|implied}}
#: {{ux|en|I gave him '''express''' instructions not to begin until I arrived, but he ignored me.}}
#: {{ux|en|This book cannot be copied without the '''express''' permission of the publisher.}}
# Truly depicted; exactly resembling.
#: {{ux|en|In my eyes it bore a livelier image of the spirit, it seemed more '''express''' and single, than the imperfect and divided countenance.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1634|author=w:John Milton|editor=w:Homer Sprague|title=The Mask of Comus|location=New York|publisher=J. W. Schermerhorn & Co.|year_published=1876|page=253|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=9XtAAAAAYAAJ&pg=PA253|passage=Soon as the potion works, their human countenance, / The '''express''' resemblance of the gods, is changed / Into some brutish form, of wolf, or bear, / Or ounce, or tiger, hog, or bearded goat, / All other parts remaining as they were{{...}}}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1805|title=The Works of Robert Leighton|author=Robert Leighton|publisher= M. Ogle|isbn=|page=169
|url=https://archive.org/details/leightonsworks02leiguoft/page/n175/mode/2up?q=express+nature|passage=
The '''express''' nature of the end, that they might ''live to God in the Spirit'': But first observe, ''it was to them that are dead.'' By which, I conceive, he intends such as had heard and believed the gospel, when it came to them, and now were dead.}}
# {{lb|en|postpositive|retail}} Providing a more limited but presumably faster service than a full or complete dealer of the same kind or type.
#: {{ux|en|Tesco '''Express'''}}
#: {{ux|en|McDonald's '''Express'''}}

